cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you publish research or results that use the corpus, please cite it as below. Use the year the corpus was accessed."
title: "The xd Crossword Corpus"
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Pwanson
    given-names: Saul
  - family-names: DeJarnatt
    given-names: Alex
url: "https://centuryarcade.org/xd/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/century-arcade/xd"
version: "2026.11"
date-released: 2026-11-06
abstract: >-
  The xd Crossword Corpus is the world's largest collection of crossword
  puzzles, with more than 160,000 published crosswords from over 160
  publications, from 1913 to today, kept in a plain-text format for research
  and preservation. Every puzzle is stored as one .xd file holding its grid,
  clues, answers and publication details, together with a record of where it
  came from for nearly every puzzle. Most puzzles are still under copyright, so the corpus itself is
  private and available for research on request.
keywords:
  - crossword
  - crossword puzzles
  - corpus
  - puzzles
  - newspapers
  - digital preservation
